{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115952",
      "title": "Accepting Parameters in Custom Pipes",
      "lectureOrder": 169,
      "videoOrder": 161,
      "sourceHash": "c4a7c414d11bc4208a4c4654f2b4a96350d96df70b646a5af2d36175475476dc",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.66,
          "end": 2.13,
          "en": "So how can we make",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 4.62,
          "en": "our own pipes configurable?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.62,
          "end": 7.5,
          "en": "Well, this transform method here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.5,
          "end": 11.97,
          "en": "is not restricted to accepting just one parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.97,
          "end": 15.03,
          "en": "It must accept at least one parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.03,
          "end": 16.77,
          "en": "because the first parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.77,
          "end": 20.253,
          "en": "is always the value after which the pipe is used.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.18,
          "end": 23.973,
          "en": "So in front of this pipe symbol here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.93,
          "end": 27.81,
          "en": "But you can then add additional parameters here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.81,
          "end": 31.32,
          "en": "to accept extra arguments for this pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.32,
          "end": 33.66,
          "en": "that make this pipe configurable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.66,
          "end": 36.27,
          "en": "And that's what all these built-in pipes do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.27,
          "end": 40.11,
          "en": "when they do accept input after this colon here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.11,
          "end": 44.46,
          "en": "the values passed thereafter are simply extra arguments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.46,
          "end": 47.16,
          "en": "passed to this transform method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.16,
          "end": 50.76,
          "en": "And here I wanna accept two extra arguments,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.76,
          "end": 53.883,
          "en": "an input type, let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.72,
          "end": 56.883,
          "en": "and an output type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.14,
          "end": 61.8,
          "en": "And both should be a string value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.8,
          "end": 64.86,
          "en": "though a string that only accepts two kinds of values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.86,
          "end": 68.82300000000001,
          "en": "cel for Celsius or fah for Fahrenheit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.02,
          "end": 72.09,
          "en": "So that's my TypeScript type definition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.09,
          "end": 73.983,
          "en": "for input and output type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.96000000000001,
          "end": 78.84,
          "en": "So these are now two extra arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.84,
          "end": 81.81,
          "en": "And indeed I wanna make the output type optional",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.81,
          "end": 85.17,
          "en": "so that if only the input type is specified,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 85.17,
          "end": 88.56,
          "en": "we know that the value does not need to be converted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.56,
          "end": 90.81,
          "en": "Whereas if both are specified,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.81,
          "end": 94.86,
          "en": "we do need to convert the value from Celsius to Fahrenheit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.86,
          "end": 96.303,
          "en": "or vice versa.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.16,
          "end": 100.28999999999999,
          "en": "So therefore now with input type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.28999999999999,
          "end": 105.21000000000001,
          "en": "and output type added as parameters to this transfer method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.21000000000001,
          "end": 107.03999999999999,
          "en": "after parsing this number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.03999999999999,
          "end": 109.97999999999999,
          "en": "before calculating the output temperature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.97999999999999,
          "end": 113.55,
          "en": "we have to add an extra if check here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.55,
          "end": 117.46000000000001,
          "en": "and check if input type is equal to Celsius",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.68,
          "end": 122.523,
          "en": "and output type is equal to Fahrenheit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 123.51,
          "end": 125.13,
          "en": "And if that's the case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 125.13,
          "end": 128.763,
          "en": "I want to calculate my temperature as I did it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 129.679,
          "end": 132.18,
          "en": "Therefore I'll add a new variable here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 132.18,
          "end": 135.813,
          "en": "output temp, which will be a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 138.12,
          "end": 140.31,
          "en": "And I'll then set it here with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 140.31,
          "end": 142.863,
          "en": "that formula inside of this F block.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 144.06,
          "end": 146.55,
          "en": "But that's just one possible case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 146.55,
          "end": 149.28,
          "en": "An alternative condition, which I want to check,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 149.28,
          "end": 152.34300000000002,
          "en": "is that input type is equal to Fahrenheit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 153.54,
          "end": 158.22,
          "en": "and output type is equal to Celsius.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 158.22,
          "end": 161.613,
          "en": "Then we want to convert the value in the opposite direction.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 162.63,
          "end": 166.916,
          "en": "So then the output temp should be equal to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 166.916,
          "end": 171.916,
          "en": "(val-32) * (5/9)",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 173.16,
          "end": 177.303,
          "en": "That's the formula for going from Fahrenheit to Celsius.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 178.71,
          "end": 180.57,
          "en": "Well, and last but not least,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 180.57,
          "end": 183.39,
          "en": "we have the same input type as output type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 183.39,
          "end": 186.18,
          "en": "or we have no output type at all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 186.18,
          "end": 189.18,
          "en": "And in both cases, the output temperature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 189.18,
          "end": 191.67,
          "en": "is equal to the input value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 191.67,
          "end": 194.763,
          "en": "because we don't need to convert anything in that case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 195.72,
          "end": 198.3,
          "en": "So with that, we got an output temperature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 198.3,
          "end": 203.07,
          "en": "but we now also need to derive this symbol dynamically here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 203.07,
          "end": 205.82999999999998,
          "en": "And for that I'll add a new variable symbol,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 205.82999999999998,
          "end": 210.82999999999998,
          "en": "which is either degrees celsius or degrees fahrenheit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 212.31,
          "end": 214.23,
          "en": "So that's again a type definition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 214.23,
          "end": 219.15,
          "en": "where I again accept exactly these two string values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 219.15,
          "end": 220.983,
          "en": "as values for a symbol.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 222.12,
          "end": 223.53,
          "en": "And I'll then set symbol",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 223.53,
          "end": 226.68,
          "en": "by checking if we don't have an output type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 226.68,
          "end": 229.32,
          "en": "So if that parameter is not provided,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 229.32,
          "end": 230.19,
          "en": "in that case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 230.19,
          "end": 233.55,
          "en": "I'll set the symbol based on the input type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 233.55,
          "end": 236.16,
          "en": "So I'll check if the input type is Celsius,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 236.16,
          "end": 239.16,
          "en": "in which case I'll pick the Celsius symbol,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 239.16,
          "end": 241.233,
          "en": "otherwise the Fahrenheit symbol.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 242.64,
          "end": 244.62,
          "en": "Else, if we do have an output type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 244.62,
          "end": 247.29,
          "en": "I'll set the symbol based on the output type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 247.29,
          "end": 249.99,
          "en": "So I'll then check if that is Celsius,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 249.99,
          "end": 254.013,
          "en": "in which case I'll set the according symbol and vice versa.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 256.11,
          "end": 257.85,
          "en": "And then it's also that symbol",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 257.85,
          "end": 260.28,
          "en": "that can be injected into this dynamically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 260.28,
          "end": 262.323,
          "en": "generated string down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 263.58,
          "end": 268.08,
          "en": "And that should then therefore give us a transform method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 268.08,
          "end": 272.46,
          "en": "that transforms the value from Celsius to Fahrenheit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 272.46,
          "end": 274.11,
          "en": "or vice versa.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 274.11,
          "end": 277.62,
          "en": "And that then also outputs the according symbol.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 277.62,
          "end": 279.51,
          "en": "And back in our template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 279.51,
          "end": 283.14,
          "en": "we therefore now have to pass at least one argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 283.14,
          "end": 287.73,
          "en": "to our pipe by adding a colon and then the argument value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 287.73,
          "end": 290.79,
          "en": "And that should be cell or Fahrenheit here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 290.79,
          "end": 294.72,
          "en": "And here I'll say that I got a temperature in Celsius,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 294.72,
          "end": 296.94,
          "en": "but I wanna output it as Fahrenheit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 296.94,
          "end": 299.34000000000003,
          "en": "And therefore I'll pass a second argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 299.34000000000003,
          "end": 301.11,
          "en": "by adding another colon here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 301.11,
          "end": 302.16,
          "en": "And after that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 302.16,
          "end": 304.59,
          "en": "we have the value for the second parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 304.59,
          "end": 306.393,
          "en": "accepted by the temp pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 307.74,
          "end": 309.54,
          "en": "We have to specify at least one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 309.54,
          "end": 313.08,
          "en": "but we can specify both because we do accept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 313.08,
          "end": 317.58299999999997,
          "en": "up to two extra arguments here on our temperature pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 319.89,
          "end": 322.14,
          "en": "Well, and with that, if we save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 322.14,
          "end": 325.443,
          "en": "this is output as Fahrenheit just as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 326.7,
          "end": 328.86,
          "en": "But if I were to switch this now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 328.86,
          "end": 331.29,
          "en": "and say that we got a value in Fahrenheit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 331.29,
          "end": 333.45,
          "en": "but it should be output in Celsius.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 333.45,
          "end": 335.64,
          "en": "If I switch that and save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 335.64,
          "end": 339.543,
          "en": "now I got a different conversion and a different value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 340.40999999999997,
          "end": 343.68,
          "en": "But we can now also see a problem here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 343.68,
          "end": 347.1,
          "en": "We have too many decimal places here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 347.1,
          "end": 350.79,
          "en": "And it would be nice if we could combine this decimal pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 350.79,
          "end": 352.83,
          "en": "with our custom pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 352.83,
          "end": 355.053,
          "en": "And thankfully we can do that.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
